# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: EDUCATION OPERATION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (EOMS)

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, product designer, UX architect, and software engineer. Build a complete, professional, responsive web application named **EOMS — Education Operation Management System**.

This is a real educational administration platform, not a static UI concept, a landing-page-only design, or a collection of disconnected dashboard mockups.

The application must provide a complete user journey:

Landing Page → Login / Registration → Role Verification → Appropriate Dashboard → Functional Modules → Logout.

Build on the existing project if source code is already present. Inspect the current files, package.json, dependencies, routing, and existing components before making changes. Preserve useful existing functionality. Do not unnecessarily replace the project or introduce incompatible dependencies.

Do not merely explain what needs to be built. Implement the application, create the necessary components, connect the navigation, and fix errors.

## 2. PRODUCT PURPOSE

EOMS helps educational institutions manage academic and administrative operations from one centralized platform.

The system supports three roles:

1. Administrator
2. Teacher
3. Student

The application must provide role-based dashboards and permissions. Each role must see relevant information, navigation items, and permitted actions.

Core modules:

- Student management
- Teacher management
- Course management
- Class and enrollment management
- Attendance
- Assignments
- Examinations and marks
- Results
- Academic reports
- Notifications
- User profile and account settings

Keep the first release practical and achievable. Implement the complete essential user journey before adding advanced features.

